B = [
('Moschino','Europe','1980s-present','fashion',"In the style of Moschino, witty, surreal, cheeky Italian pop design. Graphics are stark black and white, with a bold heavy wide sans-serif wordmark in capitals set flat on plain fields, and a second loose pink brush-script lettering in hot pink. Recurring motifs are a solid red heart, a pair of mirrored question marks inside a circle, a teddy-bear silhouette drawn in simple black and white line, and oversized playful icons. Palette is jet black, chalk white, signal red, hot pink, sunny yellow and glittering gold. Surfaces include glossy enamel, black sequins, gold foil, quilted metallic sheen and flat printed colour. Trompe-l'oeil humour turns ordinary forms into ironic, exaggerated parodies."),
('Missoni','Europe','1960s-present','fashion',"In the style of Missoni, a rhythmic textile language of zigzag chevrons, flame-stitch peaks, wavy ripples and thin stripes, knitted or woven as continuous repeating bands. Colour moves in gradual tonal steps, with rows of teal, turquoise, coral, orange, mustard, raspberry, violet, olive, cream and black blending into shimmering optical vibrations. Some versions use soft sparkling metallic threads among matte wool yarns, others are fine open crochet-like knit with tassel-like twisted ends. Patterns can run diagonally, mirror at the centre or fade from dark to light. Lettering is a small, clean, uppercase serif wordmark on a plain tab. The overall mood is warm, bohemian and artisanal, with a soft handmade hand."),
('Salvatore Ferragamo','Europe','1930s-present','fashion',"In the style of Salvatore Ferragamo, refined Florentine luxury built on a signature double-loop emblem, two mirrored open rings joined at the centre like a stylised gancio, cast in polished gold, antique brass or silver metal, or stamped in tone-on-tone relief. Materials are smooth calfskin, patent leather, suede, silk twill and grosgrain weave, in navy, black, bordeaux, nude, ivory, pale blue and soft pastel tones, often with a thin contrasting edge. Silk surfaces carry intricate painted-looking repeat prints in rich reds, blues and golds. Lettering is a slim flowing italic signature script in black or white, paired with fine spaced serif capitals. Craft details are neat hand finishing, sculpted curves and quiet, timeless elegance."),
('Brooks Brothers','North America','1900s-present','fashion',"In the style of Brooks Brothers, classic, understated American Ivy League polish. Fabrics are navy flannel, grey worsted, camel wool, oxford cloth, blue and white seersucker, madras plaid, tartan and cable-knit wool in muted tones of navy, burgundy, forest green, camel, cream and pale blue. Signature surface patterns are diagonal repp stripes in bold alternating colour bands, regimental stripes, fine pinstripes, windowpane checks and bold awning stripes, plus small repeating crests. The emblem is a golden fleece hanging within an oval, embroidered or printed in gold and navy. Lettering is traditional serif capitals, often woven into small cloth marks in a vintage cream and navy look. Details are mother-of-pearl, brass and tidy contrast piping."),
('L.L.Bean','North America','1910s-present','outdoor',"In the style of L.L.Bean, honest, rugged New England outdoor craft. Materials are heavy cotton duck canvas, brushed flannel in red, navy and green plaid checks, chunky wool knit, waxed fabric and tan or brown leather trim with bold doubled seam lines. Palette is forest green, deep navy, brick red, khaki, oatmeal cream and rust. Contrast piping and edging in a second colour add simple colour blocking. Emblem is a rectangular woven mark with cream background, a dark green border and a plain serif wordmark in capitals with a small founding date and a pine tree sketch. Details are dull brass and plain utilitarian shapes that look sturdy, practical and softly weathered."),
('Mary Quant','Europe','1960s','fashion',"In the style of Mary Quant, youthful swinging-sixties mod design. The emblem is a simple five-petal daisy with a round centre ring, drawn as a bold flat black shape on white or reversed in white, repeated in rows or scattered as a cheerful pattern in rainbow colours on black. Graphics are crisp, geometric and clean, with black and white checks, bold stripes, circles and colour blocking in red, yellow, orange, navy, turquoise and pink. Materials are shiny PVC, patent, crisp cotton, jersey and opaque coloured knit with white contrast edges. Lettering is a slim, tall, tightly spaced sans-serif in capitals, stacked in two lines. Shapes are short, tidy, simple and cut with sharp precision for a playful, modern energy."),
('Jean Paul Gaultier','Europe','1980s-present','fashion',"In the style of Jean Paul Gaultier, cheeky, theatrical Parisian pop-couture. The core pattern is navy and white horizontal Breton stripes, with variations in black, red, turquoise and pale blue. Surfaces include sheer tattoo-print mesh in sailor motifs, anchors, hearts, roses and swallows, plus pinstripe wool, corsetry satin, shiny tin metal and printed metal sheets in cream, pink and teal. Lettering is a slim hand-drawn, slightly crooked black and white wordmark in two lines, often stamped inside a stripe block or a metallic oval. Shapes mix masculine and feminine cues with cinched, sculpted curves, pointed cone silhouettes and sleek hourglass forms. Colour is witty, saucy and bold, with a playful, ironic, avant-garde attitude."),
('Fjallraven','Europe','1960s-present','outdoor',"In the style of Fjallraven, rugged, minimal Scandinavian northern design. The emblem is a bold, flat, simplified fox head with pointed ears and a sweeping cheek line in solid red, shown alone, in a circular roundel with an outer ring of text, or in tone-on-tone grey or black. Lettering is a heavy, wide, tightly set sans-serif wordmark in capitals with dotted vowels. Materials are dense waxed cotton-poly canvas, sturdy nylon and soft wool in earthy tones of khaki, olive, forest green, navy, charcoal, sand and mustard, with occasional red, orange and pale blue accents. Shapes are simple geometric blocks with straight seams, bold colour blocking and contrast seam lines."),
('Orla Kiely','Europe','2000s','homeware',"In the style of Orla Kiely, bold flat mid-century Scandinavian-inspired pattern design. Motifs are a stylised stem of oval leaves, rounded multi-petal flowers, acorns, circular blooms and overlapping ovals, repeated in neat grids, diagonal lattices and tessellated layers. Colour is warm and retro, with mustard yellow, burnt orange, olive green, chocolate brown, teal, navy, powder blue, pink and cream, often with a pop of lime or red. Shapes are simple, geometric and softly rounded, with crisp edges and no shading. Surfaces include laminated coated fabric, glossy ceramic glaze, printed cotton, embossed leather and wipe-clean prints, with tan leather trim. Lettering is a small, rounded lowercase wordmark in dark ink."),
('Cath Kidston','Europe','1990s-2010s','homeware',"In the style of Cath Kidston, sweet, cosy, nostalgic British vintage print design. Patterns are large, full-bloom cabbage roses in red, pink and blue on cream, pale duck egg green or powder blue grounds, plus tiny ditsy flowers, spots, cherries, strawberries, ticking stripes, gingham checks and quaint small repeat motifs. Prints are layered with a soft hand-drawn look and fresh, slightly faded 1950s colours of cherry red, rose pink, sky blue, mint, buttery yellow and white. Surfaces are matte cotton, glossy oilcloth, painted enamel and printed paper with red or pink trim and scalloped edges. Lettering is a small, delicate, curly cream or red script wordmark inside a neat framed rectangle."),
]
